  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Development Hoarding",
    "overview": "Helios is set like the signboard around a Malaysian development site: built to be read from the road, here from the back of a lit room on a projector. A night-ink vinyl band carries one giant sentence and the presenter's controls; white panels hold the 24-hour chart and a site plan; a zinc particulars strip states where every number comes from.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Amber always means solar",
      "Grid top-up is ink hatching",
      "Condensed heavy Archivo for distance reading",
      "Square corners, 1px hairlines, no shadows",
      "Every figure tagged REAL / EXAMPLE / STAND-IN"
    ],
